# "Reading the keyboard" — INKEY in a polling loop, five keys deep.
#
# On a video console, which is the machine the chapter's reader is sitting at
# and the one with a keyboard to poll. It also settles the case: a video case
# advances a fixed number of emulated cycles after each key rather than waiting
# on a console pattern, and reads the finished screen at the end. Every pattern
# this program offers sits in the middle of a line it is still printing, and a
# wait that lands there keeps only what had arrived by then. See ACCURACY O7.

console video
send A
send B
send C
send D
send E
screen ^ 1 YOU PRESSED A \(CODE 65\)\s*$
screen ^ 2 YOU PRESSED B \(CODE 66\)\s*$
screen ^ 3 YOU PRESSED C \(CODE 67\)\s*$
screen ^ 4 YOU PRESSED D \(CODE 68\)\s*$
screen ^ 5 YOU PRESSED E \(CODE 69\)\s*$
screen ^THAT IS FIVE\s*$
